delim-prompted
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-16
what: NoPrompt becomes a compile error for the static case. `Prompted[P]`
  is an UNINHABITED row member — "this program still needs the delimiter
  P installed" — so it costs nothing at run time and nothing handles it.
  `shift(p)` adds `Prompted[p.type]`, `push(p)` removes exactly that one
  (dependent on p, so another prompt cannot discharge it), `reset` creates
  the prompt, provides it as a given and discharges. `!.run` wants an
  empty row, so an undelimited program compiles, travels and cannot run.
  Portability without lying: `atSlot(placeholder)(prog)` turns a concrete
  prompt into a SLOT keyed by the answer type and `fill(q)` binds it by
  RE-TARGETING the captures (a walk with `over`, not a cast) — the
  operator's correction to an earlier design that weakened the type and
  kept the tree, which threw NoPrompt. The runtime NoPrompt stays for
  prompts that are not stable paths (a registry).
files: src/main/scala/Delim.scala, src/test/scala/TestDelim.scala,
  okay-llm/src/main/scala/okay/llm/Cut.scala, okay-ui/src/main/scala/okay/ui/Scope.scala,
  okay-agent/src/main/scala/okay/agent/Stepper.scala, src/jmh/scala/okay/DelimBenchmark.scala,
  specs/freer-base.md, docs/typepedia.md, CHANGELOG.md
